# Jaguar Mk2 four-door saloon, 1959-1967.
#
# The Mk2: 4,590 mm long, 1,689 mm wide, 1,448 mm high, 2,731 mm wheelbase;
# 2.4, 3.4 and 3.8 sixes, disc brakes all round, the 3.8 good for about 200 km/h.
# The strongest-evidenced 1960s sporting saloon in the section F research.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_2
#
# Colours: British Racing Green, Indigo Blue, Pearl Grey and Black are documented
# Jaguar finishes of the period.
#
# Weight: 90 in total (green 30, blue 25, grey 20, black 15).
#
# Speed 200 km/h; comfort 115/503 (line). Classes 2,3.
# Dates: 1959-1967 with a road tail to about 1980.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk2.blend. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-mk2/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=JaguarMk2(BritishRacingGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=30
intro_year=1959
intro_month=10
retire_year=1980
retire_month=6
speed=200
length=3
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=115
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=503

